<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Franco-Syrian War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1920</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Franco-Syrian War was a short conflict in 1920 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the Arab Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> proclaimed under Faisal I. When Faisal's government rejected the French mandate awarded at San Remo, French forces advanced from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a>, defeated a small Syrian army at Maysalun on 24 July 1920 and occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>, ending the kingdom and beginning the French Mandate for Syria.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/franco-syrian-war.jpg" alt="Franco-Syrian War" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown army photopgrapher, Syria, died over 70 years ago · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maysaloun2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
